Description: glwindow_eagl: retain the layer handed to update_layer()
 gst_gl_context_eagl_update_layer() releases the layer it is given, as
 gst_gl_window_eagl_get_layer() hands out a retained one. Setting a new window
 handle passed the window's own layer without a reference, so every handle set
 dropped one reference too many and the layer was freed while its view still
 held it, crashing when glimagesink removed the view.
Origin: vendor
Author: LIVI
Forwarded: not-needed
---
--- a/gst-libs/gst/gl/eagl/gstglwindow_eagl.m
+++ b/gst-libs/gst/gl/eagl/gstglwindow_eagl.m
@@ -222,6 +222,9 @@ ensure_window_handle_is_set_unlocked (GstGLWindowEagl 
     g_cond_wait (&window_eagl->priv->cond, &window_eagl->priv->draw_lock);
 
   GST_INFO_OBJECT (context, "handle set, updating layer");
+  /* update_layer() releases the layer it is given */
+  if (window_eagl->priv->layer)
+    CFRetain (window_eagl->priv->layer);
   gst_gl_context_eagl_update_layer (context, window_eagl->priv->layer);
   gst_object_unref (context);
 
